      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOCHINVAR HAWK (1) was responsible for a very good effort last time over 1800m at Globe Derby Park, finishing second and just a nose from the winner. Has the benefit of a good draw. Finds a tougher race but a win is not out of the question. CRUNCH RULES (7) scored at Port Pirie two runs ago before having his colours lowered when third at his latest appearance over 1609m at Port Pirie, beaten 6 metres. Should enjoy a nice smother from this draw and will be looking for a split at some stage. It doesn't get any easier but on his best form he is capable of a strong performance. MACHFREDDY (3) has each-way claims following a fourth at his most recent appearance over 1800m at Globe Derby Park. LARDY DAH LADY (8) is in the mix following a fifth at her most recent appearance over 1800m at Globe Derby Park.",
